faqs.a:
A.	Generally. Existing trees that are preserved on a subject property, excluding existing, individual residential lots, count towards the tree replacement requirements of this Article, provided that:
  1.	They are either:
    a.	On the approved plant list; or
    b.	Deemed of significant community value by the Director; and
  2.	They are not:
    a.	Diseased;
    b.	Poor in form;
    c.	Leaning heavily over buildings;
    d.	Too close to building foundations;
    e.	Damaging sidewalks and driveways; or
    f.	Impacting utilities.
B.	Credit for Preservation of Trees. Healthy, mature trees that are preserved on-site may count only towards trees removed.
